      "title": "Bosnian Serb nationalist Dodik declares party victory in Bosnia election",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/04/bosnian-serb-nationalist-dodik-declares-party-victory-in-bosnia-election",
      "description": "<p>Staunchly pro-Russia politician has dominated campaign and inflamed divisions despite not appearing on ballot</p><p>Bosnian Serb nationalist politician Milorad Dodik has declared victory for his party in an election in Bosnia shaped by economic pressures, the prospect of the Balkan nation joining the European Union and ethnic tensions that have divided the country since its brutal 1992-95 war.</p><p>Dodik is a staunchly pro-Russia politician who, despite not appearing on the ballot, has dominated the campaign and inflamed divisions with separatist rhetoric that has sparked fears of renewed instability in Bosnia.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/04/bosnian-serb-nationalist-dodik-declares-party-victory-in-bosnia-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
